WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.760
Today we open the door to the warm everyday words Russians use to talk about the people closest to them. I'm

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:15.540
Olya, and this is привет, Русский, episode 66. Our word of the day is MAMA. MAMA. Say it with

00:00:15.540 --> 00:00:24.460
me slowly. MAMA. Now at nature's speed, MAMA. It sounds almost exactly like the English MAMA. That

00:00:24.460 --> 00:00:29.840
is the first word many babies say everywhere. Listen to it in a sentence. My

00:00:29.840 --> 00:00:36.960
MAMA, любит чай. My month of a month loves tea. Memory hook. It sounds almost exactly

00:00:36.960 --> 00:00:43.720
like the English MAMA. The first word many babies say everywhere. Now that you know MAMA, let's

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:51.760
meet Papa. Papa, repeat after me. Papa, Papa читает книгу. Dad is reading a book. Memory

00:00:51.760 --> 00:00:59.140
hook. Just like Papa in English easy to remember. Next comes brat. Brat. Repeat after me.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:05.920
Brat. My brat играет с собакой. My brother is playing with the dog. Memory hook sounds like

00:01:05.920 --> 00:01:21.740
brat, but means they opposite a helpful brother. Our word for sister is sister, sister. Repeat

00:01:21.740 --> 00:01:29.520
Бабушка. Бабушка. Репит автами. Бабушка. Бабушка печат пирог. Гранма

00:01:29.520 --> 00:01:34.920
из бейки на пай. Memory hook. Say it like Бабушка. And picture a cozy

00:01:34.920 --> 00:01:42.260
grandma baking. Гранпа из дедушка. Диай душка. Репит автами. Дедушка. Дедушка

00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:48.780
рассказывает историю. Гранпа изделена историю. Memory hook. Диай душка. Диай

00:01:48.780 --> 00:01:55.860
парт sounds like dirt plus ушка. Сын is сын. Сын. Репит автами. Сын. У

00:01:55.860 --> 00:02:02.840
меня есть сын. I have a son. Memory hook. Short and strong like the English son. Дотор

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:08.480
из дочь. Дочь. Репит автами. Дочь. Дочь рисует картину. Дотор

00:02:08.480 --> 00:02:13.900
издровена пикчер. Memory hook. And with a soft chest sound. Say it gently.

00:02:14.620 --> 00:02:20.340
A child is ребенок. Ребенок. Репит автами. Ребенок. Ребенок

00:02:20.340 --> 00:02:27.360
играет в парке. The child is playing in the park. Memory hook. Ребенок. Think of a little

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:35.620
riaban that is your child. Parents are parents. Родители. Репит автами. Родители. Родители

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:42.160
любят детей. Parents love their children. Memory hook. Родители. The people who

00:02:42.160 --> 00:02:51.300
род give birth to you. Aunt is dirty. Тьотя. Репит автами. Тьотя. Тьотя приезжает в гости. Aunt is

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:57.220
coming to visit. Memory hook. Тьотя. Sounds bouncy and friendly. Just like a fun

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:03.660
aunt. In Russian family words often change slightly depending on who they belong to. We use

00:03:03.660 --> 00:03:10.060
my for my with masculine words like my brother. We use my for my with feminine words like

00:03:10.060 --> 00:03:15.820
моя сестра. It works like English my, but the ending must match the words gender.

00:03:16.380 --> 00:03:22.680
Мой папа sounds natural. Моя мама sounds natural too. This small change makes your sentences

00:03:22.680 --> 00:03:28.500
sound correct right away. There is something really cool about one of today's words. Brat

00:03:28.500 --> 00:03:35.380
started thousands of years ago in an ancient language as Bahéryach II. It travelled through

00:03:35.380 --> 00:03:41.200
Slavic languages and reached modern Russian almost unchanged. English brother comes from

00:03:41.200 --> 00:03:47.300
the exact same ancient route. So the two words are true cousins. In some Slavic languages,

00:03:47.680 --> 00:03:53.660
Brat can also mean body, which might surprise you. Picture to Brat sharing a brat words at

00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:59.440
a family picnic. The shared sound helps you remember they mean the same thing. In Russia

00:03:59.440 --> 00:04:04.920
families often gather for big Sunday lunches where three generations sit together. Grand

00:04:04.920 --> 00:04:10.240
parents, бабушка, и дедушка are very involved in raising children. It is common for

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:15.140
adult children to visit their parents every weekend. Do you remember what mama means?

00:04:15.820 --> 00:04:21.300
Can you say Brat out loud now? For kids, draw your family and label each person with the

00:04:21.300 --> 00:04:28.040
new Russian words. For adults, introduce your family out loud. Это моя мама, это мой папа.

00:04:28.400 --> 00:04:34.840
Say it three times. Remember, поезди from a few lessons ago. Try this. Моя семья едет

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:40.480
на поезде. You did great today. Say today's words out loud one more time and there yours.

